    "holland_valley": [
      {
        "id": "stash_hv_01",
        "name": "Deep Dive",
        "location": "Laurel Residence, directly west of Rye & Son's Aviation",
        "required_gear": "None",
        "unique_rewards": null,
        "clue_notes": [
          "My darling hubby, the bunker’s flooded… AGAIN! We were gonna use the stuff in there to help The Resistance. Where’d you put the shed key? I’ll go turn on the water pump. - Wifey",
          "Wifey: We’re not gonna drain the bunker in time. I packed up the car with supplies, we’ll have to run before the cult gets here. We’ll have to leave whatever’s down there. Doubt the Peggies can hold their breath long enough to get their hands on the key to the shed - Hubby"
        ],
        "alternative_methods": null,
        "guide": "Read the note inside the house on the kitchen counter. Go out to the backyard shed, open the hatch beside it, and climb down the ladder into the water. Swim through the flooded bunker to grab the keycard off the desk at the far end. Return to the surface, unlock the shed with the keycard, and activate the yellow water pump switch by the window. Head back down into the drained bunker and smash through the wooden boards to access the stash."
      },
      {
        "id": "stash_hv_02",
        "name": "D.I.Y. and D.O.A.",
        "location": "Doverspike Compound, foot of the mountains in northwest Holland Valley",
        "required_gear": "None",
        "unique_rewards": null,
        "clue_notes": [
          "Hey'you stupid cultist f**ks! You’ll never get into my bunker. It’s impregnable. I built it myself. But even if you do, you’ll never get back out again.",
          "Les, baby, I don’t know what those idiots from Hilgard Electric were so uptight about. you don’t need a “degree” in “electrical engineering” or anything else. You an’ me built this bunker with our bare hands. Safety hazard my entire ass. Didn’t I get a smoke detector and a sprinkler system from Red’s place last month? We’re gonna be fine down here."
        ],
        "alternative_methods": null,
        "guide": "Read the clue next to the shed door to the left of the house. Head inside the main house to the back bedroom dresser to retrieve the shed key. Unlock the shed, open the hatch, and descend into the bunker. Follow the hallway to the left, take a quick right to the end of the room, and pull the yellow generator switch inside the closet. Navigate back through the hallway carefully while avoiding fire, traps, and hazards, then swipe the keycard reader to open the bunker door."
      },
      {
        "id": "stash_hv_03",
        "name": "Dumpster Diving",
        "location": "Waste treatment facility in the hills north of Fall's End",
        "required_gear": "Grapple",
        "unique_rewards": null,
        "clue_notes": [
          "Dodd’s nowhere to be found. I’m sure he won’t mind if we stash some stuff in the back office. Power’s not hooked up quite right, so watch your step if you turn it on."
        ],
        "alternative_methods": null,
        "guide": "Read the note outside the manager's trailer. Shoot the explosive red barrel on top of the stacked container to clear debris, climb onto the trailer roof, and jump across the perimeter wall. Cross the red container with the plywood plank to reach the center crates, then grapple-swing from the next container to the opposite ledge. Drop into the flooded basement below and activate the power switch on the north wall by the green tanks. Turn around, jump across the high shelving to avoid the electrified water, leap over the chainlink fence to the wall top, drop down onto the wooden beams, and open the stash door."
      },
      {
        "id": "stash_hv_04",
        "name": "Fire in the Hole",
        "location": "Cabin above Orville Creek, far southeast Holland Valley",
